<header><p class="st-kicker">republic · Egypt, North Africa and Sudan</p><h1 class="st-title">Republic of Salé</h1><p class="st-meta">1627 CE – 1668 CE · capital Rabat</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">A corsair republic of Morisco exiles at the mouth of the Bou Regreg, whose ships raided from the Atlantic coasts to Iceland.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/moriscos">Moriscos</a> expelled from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spain">Spain</a> between 1609 and 1614, among them the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hornacheros">Hornacheros</a> from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/extremadura">Extremadura</a>, settled in the kasbah of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rabat">Rabat</a> opposite <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sale">Salé</a>. In 1627 they declared independence from the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/saadi-sultanate">Saadi Sultanate</a>, forming a self-governing corsair state.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>The republic was ruled by a council, the divan, and an elected governor. Its corsairs, including the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dutch">Dutch</a> renegade <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jan-janszoon">Jan Janszoon</a>, known as Murat Reis, raided European shipping and coasts, and in 1627 raiders reached <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/republic-of-iceland">Iceland</a>. Captives were ransomed or sold, and European powers signed treaties and bombarded the port in turn. Feuds divided the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hornacheros">Hornacheros</a> and later Andalusi settlers.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>From 1641 the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/dilaiyya">Dila'iyya</a> dominated <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sale">Salé</a>, and in 1668 the Alaouite ruler <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/al-rashid-of-morocco">Moulay al-Rashid</a> took the twin towns. Corsairing continued under the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/alaouite-sultanate">Alaouite Sultanate</a> into the 19th century.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/republic-of-sale.jpg" alt="Republic of Salé" width="320" height="213"><figcaption>Image: Dekodrak · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_the_Republic_of_Sal%C3%A9_(1624-1668).svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1627 CE – 1668 CE</dd><dt>Century</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/17th-century">17th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>republic</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>mercantile</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Rabat</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Jan Janszoon</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Sunni Islam</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Spanish, Arabic</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/morocco">Morocco</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Republic of Bou Regreg, Corsair Republic of Salé</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1648&amp;focus=republic-of-sale" aria-label="Republic of Salé on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="4506 945 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Republic of Salé lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M4826 1201L4873 1200M4826 1201L4858 1205"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M4873 1200h0M4858 1205h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M4826 1201h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M4826 1201h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Rabat. <a href="/atlas?year=1648&amp;focus=republic-of-sale">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
